{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"code\": \"def check_replication_health(measured_lag_ms: float, threshold_ms: float) -> dict:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Check whether replication lag is within the acceptable threshold.\\n\\n    BUG_51: the threshold comparison is wrong — it converts\\n    threshold_ms to seconds while measured_lag_ms remains in\\n    milliseconds, so the check almost never triggers.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    exceeded = measured_lag_ms > threshold_ms\\n    if exceeded:\\n        import orgops\\n\\n        orgops.alerts.notify(\\n            \\\"replication_lag_exceeded\\\",\\n            measured_lag_ms=measured_lag_ms,\\n            threshold_ms=threshold_ms,\\n        )\\n    return {\\n        \\\"measured_lag_ms\\\": measured_lag_ms,\\n        \\\"threshold_ms\\\": threshold_ms,\\n        \\\"exceeded\\\": exceeded,\\n    }\\n\", \"comments\": \"Compare the lag and threshold in the same units and call orgops.alerts.notify whenever the check reports an exceeded condition.\"}"}}
